VRS Simulator — FTC Quick Notes
VRS (Virtual Robot Simulator): Practice FTC programming without a physical robot.
Programming: Supports Java and Blocks.
Hardware: Use the exact motor/servo names from the VRS robot.
Tank Drive: Our robot uses frontLeft and frontRight.
Motor Direction: Reverse one side if the robot spins instead of driving straight.
TeleOp: Driver controls the robot with the gamepad.
Autonomous: Robot performs a programmed sequence by itself.
Functions: Create commands like forward(), backward(), left(), and right().
Telemetry: Displays information to help find programming errors.
Encoders: Used for more accurate distances and turns.
Sensors: Can be used to make the robot react to its surroundings.
Practice: Start with simple movements → challenges → full autonomous.
Important: Always test one movement at a time before combining them.
